      "content": "General Information",
      "contentHtml": null
    },
    {
      "id": "c9a86f45-6887-ef11-8474-000d3a37e3b6",
      "type": "GeneralText",
      "area": "General",
      "position": 2,
      "content": "This agreement displays all lower-division courses required in the major: CSU Northridge courses on the left, approved (articulated) transfer courses to the right. General education (Cal-GETC or CSU Northridge GE) and upper-division courses are also required to complete the bachelor's degree. Completion of all coursework listed in this agreement is not mandatory prior to admission. For CSU Northridge Undergraduate Admission Requirements , refer to Upper Division Transfer . Some coursework may be satisfied by Advanced Placement exams completed in high school. Visit AP Credit for information. Additional information about the major is available in the CSUN University Catalog . Questions regarding this agreement may be directed to: articulation@csun.edu .",
      "contentHtml": "<p><strong>This agreement displays all lower-division courses required in the major:</strong> CSU Northridge courses on the left, approved (articulated) transfer courses to the right. General education (Cal-GETC or CSU Northridge GE) and upper-division courses are also required to complete the bachelor's degree.</p><p><br></p><p>Completion of all coursework listed in this agreement is not mandatory prior to admission. For CSU Northridge Undergraduate <strong>Admission Requirements</strong>, refer to <a href=\"http://www.csun.edu/admissions-records/apply-upper-division-transfer-student#eligible\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Upper Division Transfer</a>.</p><p><br></p><p>Some coursework may be satisfied by Advanced Placement exams completed in high school. Visit <a href=\"http://catalog.csun.edu/policies/advanced-placement-ap-credit/\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">AP Credit</a> for information. Additional information about the major is available in the <a href=\"http://catalog.csun.edu/programs/major/\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">CSUN University Catalog</a>.</p><p><br></p><p>Questions regarding this agreement may be directed to: <a href=\"mailto:articulation@csun.edu\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">articulation@csun.edu</a>.</p>"
    },
    {
      "id": "faa96f45-6887-ef11-8474-000d3a37e3b6",
      "type": "GeneralTitle",
      "area": "General",
      "position": 3,
      "content": "Pre-Clinical Phase",
      "contentHtml": null
    },
    {
      "id": "f0a96f45-6887-ef11-8474-000d3a37e3b6",
      "type": "GeneralText",
      "area": "General",
      "position": 4,
      "content": "All entering undergraduates are regarded as Pre-Clinical Phase students. Evaluation for admission to Clinical Privileges includes faculty assessment and satisfactory completion of upper-division Pre-clinical Phase courses at CSU Northridge. If a student is denied admission to Clinical Privileges it is possible to complete the baccalaureate degree as a non-clinical major. See catalog for further details. The program offers an emphasis in either Audiology or Speech-Language Pathology.",
      "contentHtml": "<p>All entering undergraduates are regarded as Pre-Clinical Phase students. Evaluation for admission to Clinical Privileges includes faculty assessment and satisfactory completion of upper-division Pre-clinical Phase courses at CSU Northridge. If a student is denied admission to Clinical Privileges it is possible to complete the baccalaureate degree as a non-clinical major. See catalog for further details.</p><p><br></p><p>The program offers an emphasis in either Audiology or Speech-Language Pathology.</p>"
    }
  ],
